        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "93c3cc84-ca77-507a-86a1-30f27af7da81",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Moominpappa at Sea, The Old Man and the Sea, Moominvalley in November\n- People: Ernest Hemingway\n- Places: Bimini, Bahamas\n- Topics: literary references, publication, series chronology\n\nFacts:\n- In 1951, Ernest Hemingway wrote The Old Man and the Sea in Bimini, Bahamas.\n- In 1952, The Old Man and the Sea was published.\n- Moominpappa at Sea has an original title that loosely references Ernest Hemingway's novel The Old Man and the Sea, but this reference is not reflected in translation.\n- In 1965, Moominpappa at Sea was published before or contemporaneously with Moominvalley in November.\n- Moominvalley in November is set contemporaneously with Moominpappa at Sea.\n- Moominvalley in November is the only installment in the series in which the Moomin family are absent.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
